Subject: Preserve original string algorithms with native temporary Data alignment

Upstream-base: 11c0bc65ad2ec21431c5d74f1ac4cbc1e3e2e2c3

Carry the native pointer field of Vector<T, TempStringPoolAllocator> as byte-safe
four-byte-aligned storage beneath the original methods. Retain the original
four-byte payload prefix, allocation/free thresholds, counts and growth; refuse
unreviewed over-aligned element types. Literal original insert/erase methods are
used by genuine native source. Historical native insertion policies remain only
under the explicit diagnostic vector profile. The port-owned pointer carrier
rejects mixing that profile with an original game module.

This is runtime native object ABI, not serialized Wii data. It does not restore
the separate TempStringAllocator manager or qualify source CRT/static teardown.

